# Planning

When you **author or extend** an implementation plan (Cursor plan mode,
`.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`, or a multi-step agent brief for EnvyBot), the
plan is incomplete unless it includes **both** sections below in addition to
the feature work. Do not ship a plan that is feature-only.

## 1. High-value technical debt cleanup pass

Add a scoped subsection and matching todos. Prefer **cheap structural wins**
that make the feature honest (shared sqlite conn, import boundaries, batch
reads, docs/tests). **Defer** heavy refactors explicitly (large file splits,
optional perf work) with a one-line reason, not silence.

Each debt item should state **what** and **why now** (blocks the feature,
reduces duplicate paths, or pays down active confusion). Skip drive-by
reformatting and unrelated refactors.

## 2. Greenfield migration

Add a subsection aligned with [`.cursor/rules/greenfield.mdc`](greenfield.mdc).

- **Book check** before removing product migrators: confirm operator book(s)
  have no leftover files/keys the migrator handled; confirm one-shot meta
  stamps where applicable.
- **One-shot cleanup** in the operator session (inline Python only; do not
  commit migration scripts).
- **Product code** opens the canonical shape only; delete `migrate_*`, open-time
  backfills, dual-read, and compatibility shims in the **same change set** as
  the cleanup, after the book check passes.
- Update command docs (`docs/commands/`) when storage or fleet load behavior
  changes.

Order debt and greenfield relative to the feature as the plan requires
(often: finish product surface, book check, then strip migrators). Always
list verification (tests, `./envybot fleet` smoke) in the plan.

## Plan frontmatter

Use plan todos for debt and greenfield items (distinct ids). Cancel or mark
deferred items explicitly rather than omitting the section.
